ense ÷ revenue (lower is better).","Figures are from StockAnalysis (S&P Global Market Intelligence data) for fiscal years ended Dec 31, 2025 and a year earlier. Never estimated: items not reported there are left out.","Diluted EPS by quarter as reported in the 10-Qs; fourth quarters are calculated (net income ÷ estimated diluted shares) because EPS does not add across quarters.","Percentages are of revenue; figures may not sum due to rounding."],"report":{"summary":["BOK Financial is a regional bank holding company based in Oklahoma that offers commercial banking, consumer banking and wealth management. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 6.1% to $2.2B in 2025. Net interest income rose 9.6% to $1.3B and noninterest income rose 1.1% to $849M; noninterest expense rose 6.1%, and the provision for credit losses was $2.0M, versus $18.0M.","Net income to common rose 10.7% to $574M, or $9.17 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 66.3% versus 66.3%. BOK Financial returned $567M through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 6.1% to $2.2B.","Net interest income rose 9.6%.","Noninterest income rose 1.1% to $849M.","Net income to common rose 10.7% to $574M."],"watch":["Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was $1.4B, up 6.1%.","Credit-loss provision was $2.0M."],"table":[["Total revenue",2.1764,2.0504,1],["Net interest income",1.3273,1.2108],["Noninterest income",0.8491,0.8396],["Noninterest expense",1.4435,1.3602],["Provision for credit losses",0.002,0.018],["Other items, net",0.0097,-0.0055],["Pre-tax income",0.7406,0.6666,1],["Income tax",0.1626,0.1431],["Noncontrolling interests",0.0,0.0],["Other adjustments",-0.004,0.005],["Net income to common",0.574,0.5186,1],["Diluted EPS ($)",9.165747,8.135183,0,"eps"],["Book value per share ($)",97.634386,86.529017,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["BOK Financial Corporation Form 10-K filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK